Roboto Condensed
----------------
    Copyright 2015 Google Inc.
    Apache License 2.0 -- `tools/fonts/Apache-2.0.txt`, `LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt`
    https://github.com/googlefonts/roboto-condensed

Vendored unmodified at `tools/fonts/RobotoCondensed-Regular.ttf`.

The guest type rasteriser does not read that file at run time; it is a build-host
input. `tools/gen_typeface.py` walks its `cmap`, `glyf`, `loca` and `hmtx` tables
and emits the outline coordinates as a static table, which the bare-metal guest can
afford to pay for byte by byte. The generated table is therefore a work derived from
Google's font, and it says so in its own header:

    sdk/rust/interos-std/src/design/face.rs

Nothing else in this repository comes from a third-party work.

Fetched at run time, not distributed
------------------------------------
Device Studio loads two front-end libraries that are not part of this source tree
and are not licensed to you by us:

    noVNC              MPL-2.0   npm `@novnc/novnc` ^1.7.0
    Lucide icon set    ISC       npm `lucide` ^1.47.0

They are resolved from `emulator/node_modules` when installed locally, and Lucide
falls back to a CDN copy in the browser (`emulator/index.html`). Obtain them from
their own projects under their own licences.

Formats, not code
-----------------
The decoders in `sdk/rust/interos-std` implement published specifications (PNG, GIF,
baseline JPEG, WebP, WAV, X.509, TLS, GGUF) written from scratch with no reference
implementation vendored. Fixtures under `sdk/rust/interos-std/tests/fixtures/` are
generated here; those that model a hostile or malformed input are named for the
property they test.

Model weights
-------------
No model weights are distributed with this source. A GGUF file, if provisioned, is
obtained separately and stays under the licence its distributor states; the repository
carries the reader, not the weights.
